/-! # Descent at TRAINED weights — the MLP's input layer

The net is `MlpWitness`'s: Chapter 2's architecture at width 8 on the 28×28 image,
`dense 784→8 → relu → dense 8→8 → relu → dense 8→10`, bias-free, trained on MNIST and
rationalized to `k/128` (`TrainedMlp.W0V`, `W1V`, `W2V`, imported, not re-emitted). The
example is MNIST test image #63, all 784 pixels, `k/255`: a 3 the net reads as a 2.

**One SGD step with the exact gradient on the input weights `W₀`, at learning rate
`2⁻35`, decreases that example's cross-entropy loss by at least `lr·‖∇L‖₂²/2`**
(`trained_mlp_input_sgd_descends_concrete`): `mlp_input_sgd_descends` at `η = 0`, `a = 1`,
`w₁ = 228/128`, `w₂ = 280/128`, every hypothesis discharged. The step crosses both ReLU
layers, so the theorem needs both sign patterns frozen along it; the margins are read off
the exact pre-activations (`pre0_eq`: 8 units on, 0 off; `pre1_eq`: 6 on, 2 off),
each 784-term sum one kernel evaluation over `List ℤ` numerators (`Foundation/ListDot`).

The window needs `Σ|∇|` from above and `Σ∇²` from below, and the gradient holds a softmax.
No `exp` is evaluated. By `mlp_input_loss_gradAt` the gradient is the outer product
`∇[i,k] = xᵢ·c_k`, `c = mask⁰ ⊙ W₁(mask¹ ⊙ W₂(p − onehot))` (`grad_key`), so the sums factor
as `(Σxᵢ)·Σ|c_k|` and `(Σxᵢ²)·Σc_k²`. Each `c_k` is a fixed rational combination of the ten
softmax entries (`backC_0` … `backC_7`), and `p` is a probability vector, so
`|c_k| ≤ max_j |G_kj − G_k,lbl|` (`cot_abs_le`), which gives `gradL1_le`. For the lower bound
the image is MISCLASSIFIED: `z_3 ≤ z_2` is a rational inequality (`hz_lbl_le`), so
`p_3 ≤ 1/2` by monotonicity of `exp` alone (`sm_lbl_le_half`); row 4 of `G` has all nine
differences `G_4,j − G_4,3` of one sign, so `|c_4| ≥ 30629/16384·(1 − p_3)` (`cot_lower`), which
gives `gradSq_lower`.

The drop is therefore strictly positive (`trained_mlp_input_sgd_strictly_descends`, `<`),
by at least `lr·S2lb/2 ≈ 9.11e-10`. What is not shown: the gradient is exact (no float
model, unlike `LinearDescent`), the step moves `W₀` only, and it is one example, not a batch.

Generated by `scripts/certs/trained_mlp_descent.py`; weights and input are DATA. -/

